 "response": "Getosti's budget is now **$2,075K**.\n\n**How I got there**\n\n- **Which records count:** only Finance Office budget updates change the budget, so I ignored all other messages. I also ignored Finance Office records that don't change the amount, such as cost center codes, room moves and audit notes.\n- **Starting point:** #0001 set the budget to $1,730K.\n- **Withdrawals:** I followed every withdrawal chain to its end. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, which revives the item it had targeted. For example:\n  - #0002 (+$472K) still applies. The chain #0007 \u2190 #0009 \u2190 #0015 \u2190 #0032 \u2190 #0081 \u2190 #0161 ends with #0161 standing, so #0007's withdrawal of #0002 is cancelled.\n  - #0003 (+$547K) is removed. In the chain #0012 \u2190 #0013 \u2190 #0021 \u2190 #0154 \u2190 #1164, #1164 stands, so #0012's withdrawal of #0003 holds.\n  - #0206 (\u2212$576K) is removed. In #0297 \u2190 #0402 \u2190 #0682, #0682 cancels #0402, so #0297 withdraws #0206.\n  - #0568 (+$18K) is removed. In #0812 \u2190 #1477 \u2190 #1491, #1491 cancels #1477, so #0812 withdraws #0568.\n  - #0431 (\u2212$51K) still applies. In #0528 \u2190 #0756 \u2190 #0848 \u2190 #0938, #0938 cancels #0848, so #0756 stands and cancels #0528.\n- **Calculation:** I applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in record order, starting from $1,730K. The total comes to $2,075K.\n\nANSWER: $2075K",
